{"id": "EUVD-2026-76464", "enisaUuid": "b964f675-f193-3ac9-9109-cb77351847db", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnouveau/gem: reserve the bo in the info ioctl around the vma lookup\n\nIn the non-uvmm path, there could be a race between the info lookup\nfinding the vma, and the gem close path closing the vma leading\nto a use-after-free.\n\nSpotted with the help of Opus 4.6.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:44:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:48:46", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e05c28bd6043d0fd0bea9c3fc49300a8871a1a81", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/208867763843aa82efcbe3b771f1b8e6c7aa820a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ff110e85837d7ecd83f36078107be240ff5ae409", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e60466011ac3a6b8045e6cc3c2cbb30d58039d2e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5e17160d41d92823f3379c1982e1369680c5ce4d"], "aliases": ["GHSA-9qfh-2fg7-437p", "CVE-2026-89553"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0d44ce97-b527-3606-949a-c23e3c81e8f0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.109"}, {"id": "3873b892-316a-3247-bbe1-36b07870008d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e758a3111914af7ee4351be86f1ac0efe87ed06e <ff110e85837d7ecd83f36078107be240ff5ae409"}, {"id": "511203ca-f609-352f-921f-c330ab040909", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.1"}, {"id": "610cc462-c2a6-3837-9584-407e73eb1929", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e758a3111914af7ee4351be86f1ac0efe87ed06e <e05c28bd6043d0fd0bea9c3fc49300a8871a1a81"}, {"id": "6e0e5570-22a3-3efa-8ea1-3c95dc0cda5f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "6f5359b5-a7de-3dc9-b